think Designed the crux: reading-order betweenness (a STRICT TOTAL order, so exactly one of any three groups is the reading-middle) and spatial bounding-box betweenness (a PARTIAL relation over the plane, so a triple can have NO spatial middle) are DIFFERENT relations that differ in KIND -- the box-is-a-prefilter lesson lifted to a TRIPLE, a span box OVER-CLAIMING the between the order names exactly.
think Built ONE 20x20 scene of six singletons yielding all four verdicts by choosing triples: P rank 1, V a TALL block rank 2, W rank 3, Q rank 4, S rank 5, R rank 6 (ranks keyed on top edge then left edge, all keys distinct so deterministic). BOTH (P,Q,R diagonal), ORDER_ONLY (P,V,R -- V's tall box escapes the span on x), SPACE_ONLY (V,S,W -- the tall V stretches the span box down over S while the page order seats S after both), NEITHER (P,R,Q). Plus totality of the reading middle over P,Q,R and NO spatial middle at all over Q,R,S (an L).
